# fresh_host_map_memory_refused_root: The root node's map_memory returns false: DeviceCore::set_root_page calls destroy_task on the root task but keeps its handle (only its base is cleared), and leaves no root node. A root FIFO set up then calls no block (there is no root node to hang it on): the enable reads back 0 and the NOP never completes, with no fault. Writing the root page again creates a new task (the kept, destroyed one is simply replaced, never destroyed again) and the device works.
